{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do","id":1093937,"title":"\"Silver Fangs\" PB 2 & Under - where do they go, what do they do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-17T18:38:22-07:00","id":1093937,"title":"\"Silver Fangs\" PB 2 & Under - where do they go, what do they do?","content":"Silver Fangs require minimum Pure Breed 3. We also know that the tribe has taken various desperate attempts to preserve as much Pure Breed as they can. The implication is that there is a not insignificant amount of Garou of Silver Fang stock who &quot;fall out&quot; of Falcon's favor because they lack the requisite Pure Breed. These Garou have to become members of another tribe. Yet I can't recall this situation ever being addressed in the source materials even though this has to be a factor in the game setting. Here are my thoughts on how this should be handled.<br /> <br /> 1) I don't think this a significant amount of Garou in the sense that the Silver Fangs are hemorrhaging members, but I do think it would be large enough to be noticeable and impact tribal politics.<br /> <br /> 2) What about the tribes they join?<br /> a)I think we can identify a lot of tribes such Garou won't be joining. No Bone Gnawers, Uktena, or Wendigo. I don't see any desire of SFs who would join the BG, and I don't think the Pure Ones would accept any. Because their numbers are already extremely low, I think Silent Striders and Stargazers are also out.<br /> b) There are some tribes a few members might join, but probably would not be in great numbers. These would be Glass Walkers, Black Furies, and Children of Gaia. Each tribe is very focused on a particular mindset that I feel the overwhelming mass of such Garou would not want to join them. They may have a few odd ducks here and there as curiosities.<br /> c) I think most such Garou would join only a few tribes: Fianna, Get of Fenris, Shadow Lords, and Red Talons (for the lupus among them). These tribes have a real sense of tradition, strong ties to the Silver Fangs traditionally, and are strongly associated with certain SF royal houses. I imagine the Fianna would be the tribe of choice for most Silver Fangs from Western Europe, and the Shadow Lords for those in Russia and Asia. A fair number still go to the Get and Talons, but because those tribes are far harsher, there is probably a noticeable drop off compared to the big two.<br /> <br /> 3) What about the Pure Breed of these tribal newcomers? Technically speaking, I imagine their PB would be set to zero if it is &quot;totem specific.&quot; However, I also feel that since the Silver Fangs are are the original tribe and first heroes of the Garou, that the other tribes' features probably accept them to a certain degree so that if they are PB 2 or 1, they retain that even if in another tribe. Exceptions made for Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers since their totems are so spiritually polluting that it kills PB dead.<br /> <br /> 4) There have to be older lineages of well established &quot;ex-Silver Fangs&quot; in some of the tribes back from the days when the Silver Fangs cast out those didn't meet their exact standards. I imagine there are various dynasties among the Fianna, Shadow Lords, Red Talons, and Get of Fenris who trace their origins back to the SF even if they are now thoroughly bred in with the tribe.<br /> <br /> 5) This creates an interesting dynamic. Are such cast offs residually loyal to the SFs (I imagine many Fianna and Get newcomers would be)? Resentful and angry (I imagine those that are would flock to the Shadow Lords)? What about their distant ties to the SFs? Do they see them as still proud and honorable in the modern days, or glad they are not part of a decrepit falling tribe? I think it all depends on the individuals, but clearly this would add some complexity to tribal politics.<br /> <br /> 6) What about within the tribe? How do the older/original members of those tribes feel? I think how Shadow Lords would treat such members to be very different from the Fianna and Get of Fenris. Anything from being welcoming of receiving such royal blood, to viewing them as incompetents losers, bastards with potential, or just another green recruit.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to your comments and your own ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-18-2017, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T19:59:54-07:00","id":1093959,"title":"","content":"Kinfolk a Breed Apart says on page 15 that when a new child is born to the Fangs, his mother is interviewed and various magics are worked to verify his paternity.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that occasionaly exemptions are made in cases of arranged marriages with other tribes or carefully negotiated breeding arrangements with wolf Kinfolk...<br /> <br /> Otherwise...if they find the Father is not of Silver Fang blood, they take the child away.<br /> <br /> the official story, is that their placed with foster parents less particular about breeding, and it says most garou would prefer to believe the official story... implying that their just killed.<br /> <br /> You can go with either... and it can vary I think, on if a particular sept leader has a soft or hard heart...<br /> <br /> Incidently... it does list the Bone Gnawers as one of the tribes they might offer the child to... but I find that I agree with you...<br /> <br /> I doubt the Fangs would want to give the gnawers even their cast off Bastards.<br /> <br /> Same reason I doubted they'd hire a Gnawer Kinfolk to work as a maid on their estate...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1080443-subtle-displays-of-wealth\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...lays-of-wealth</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-18-2017, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:17:19-07:00","id":1094141,"title":"","content":"Offing a cub with too low a pedigree isn't just hard-hearted, but dumb beyond dumb, of the kind that the tribe probably stopped a long time ago. Not long enough ago, perhaps, but almost definitely not modern practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:34:43-07:00","id":1094149,"title":"","content":"I said thats what it implied in the book not that I condoned it...<br /> <br /> thoughts on my argument, they'd not want to offer even their castoff bastards to the bone gnawers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-18-2017, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:07:28-07:00","id":1094198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094149#post1094149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said thats what it implied in the book not that I condoned it...<br /> <br /> thoughts on my argument, they'd not want to offer even their castoff bastards to the bone gnawers?</div> </div> </div> </div>A) <i>Anyone</i> but the Bone Gnawers<br /> B) The Bone Gnawers will take <i>Anyone</i>, even those bastard Silver Fangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:07:54-07:00","id":1094199,"title":"","content":"Giving their unwanted kids to the Bone Gnawers makes the absolute most sense for one simple reason:<br /> <br /> The Gnawers don't care about lineage, and they're not going to raise their adopted kids to care about lineage. Give them to the Gnawers while they're still too young to know any better, and they'll grow up a Gnawer with no knowledge of their true ancestry, and no desire to find out. The Gnawers are &quot;mutts&quot; with all sorts of lineages already mixed in, so a white coat isn't going to scream, &quot;they must be a Silver Fang!&quot; or merit any real curiosity. The Silver Fang Houses also represent a wider array of ethnic groups than most of the other Tribes. It's a lot easier to find a Middle Eastern Gnawer to take in a cub of House Wise Heart than it would be to find a Get of the proper looks.<br /> <br /> Any Tribe with Pure Breed is a tribe that cares about lineage on some levels, which means a Silver Fang cast off is going to get curious about their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:17:52-07:00","id":1094207,"title":"","content":"Children of Gaia adopt everyone even spirals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:42:41-07:00","id":1094220,"title":"","content":"Pure Breed 2 is like Spock among the Vulcans.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://pics.onsizzle.com/spock-to-humans-spock-to-vulcans-aint-nobody-teus-me-9743084.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> What's a dirty mongrel to the Silver Fangs is an incredibly rare and noble-looking aristocrat to everyone else. Bone Gnawers would reject a Garou that had ANY pure breed too because that's in their manifesto.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T12:04:19-07:00","id":1094252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094220#post1094220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure Breed 2 is like Spock among the Vulcans.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://pics.onsizzle.com/spock-to-humans-spock-to-vulcans-aint-nobody-teus-me-9743084.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> What's a dirty mongrel to the Silver Fangs is an incredibly rare and noble-looking aristocrat to everyone else. Bone Gnawers would reject a Garou that had ANY pure breed too because that's in their manifesto.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they reject a garou with PB? The revised tb even has a merit specifically for having noble blood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T12:05:50-07:00","id":1094253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094252#post1094252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would they reject a garou with PB? The revised tb even has a merit specifically for having noble blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same way Bone Gnawers can't have Resources? The whole point of the tribe is they reject the trappings of wealth, power, and prestige. It's like asking why Black Furies would reject Male Homids or Lupus.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T12:12:26-07:00","id":1094255,"title":"","content":"I imagine any cast offs know they are from Silver Fang stock because until they have the First Change, they don't know what level of Pure Breed the Garou cub will have. That kinfolk family lineage may have reliably produced litters of PB 3 Garou, but at some point a son or daughter has their first Garou child, and fifteen years later it becomes apparent the line (from that individual at least) is now PB 2 and the other Silver Fangs recoil - no more mating with that kinfolk family, ship them off to somewhere. The kinfolk family and Garou obviously know where their lineage comes from, but they're treated like bastards and not part of the family anymore.<br /> <br /> If that wasn't an issue of lines slowly losing the PB needed, I don't think there'd be the ridiculous inbreeding the tribe is known for. This isn't the case of SF fooling around with someone else (although that is always the possibility), but simple genetic drift as certain aspects are lost over time.<br /> <br /> Only in very unusual situations would a Garou from a Silver Fang line not already know that is their heritage<br /> <br /> I see no reason why Bone Gnawers would be a preferred destination for these cast offs. What kinfolk or Garou parents would want their child adopted by Rat? They would go from the alpha to the omega tribe, have terrible peers (compared to their social ties and cultural expectations beforehand), lose all contact with their Ancestors and likely stick out like a sore thumb in terms of culture. If a Silver Fang from the Middle East is looking for a tribe and can't find one of the ones I find most likely (although I'd imagine Shadow Lords being close by and there might even be a few small pockets of Fianna and even Get whose regional origins are from the days of the Classical World), tribes like the Children of Gaia are fairly ubiquitous and would be much more preferred than the Bone Gnawers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T12:16:40-07:00","id":1094256,"title":"","content":"I think Children of Gaia may be preferred. since they wont make an issue if the cub grows up to join another tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T12:26:09-07:00","id":1094261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094253#post1094253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The same way Bone Gnawers can't have Resources? The whole point of the tribe is they reject the trappings of wealth, power, and prestige. It's like asking why Black Furies would reject Male Homids or Lupus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in character creation states that Bone Gnawers don't accept purebred cubs, just that they don't have the pb after joining. Granted, how the Gnawers are written is pretty suspeect (made a thread about it here).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I think you are thinking about it too mechanically. Most rejected cubs join Gnawers because after being kicked out of their tribe, Gnawers are the first to offer them kindness and shelter. Remember that these cubs most likely knew the Nation only through the lens of the tribe they were born to, and being rejected meant they felt shame and were lost. While low pb garou cubs can be given to Children of Gaia, ones that fail the Rite of Passage or somehow shame themselves before their rite don't have that chance of being acclimated to a new tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T13:23:47-07:00","id":1094282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094261#post1094261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are thinking about it too mechanically. Most rejected cubs join Gnawers because after being kicked out of their tribe, Gnawers are the first to offer them kindness and shelter. Remember that these cubs most likely knew the Nation only through the lens of the tribe they were born to, and being rejected meant they felt shame and were lost. While low pb garou cubs can be given to Children of Gaia, ones that fail the Rite of Passage or somehow shame themselves before their rite don't have that chance of being acclimated to a new tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're talking about two very different scenarios. The type of Garou you are talking about are the screw ups and failures who can't hack it as Garou of other tribes. They may not have many options to go. Other tribes may not want them at all. However, in the &quot;They would Be Silver Fangs if they weren't PB2&quot; scenario, there is no indication that such Garou are screw ups or failures. Their only &quot;flaw&quot; is that they don't have PB 3. They may not be good enough for the Silver Fangs because of pedigree issues, but I actually think most other tribes would love to have them. They'd be high in demand.<br /> <br /> In other words, there is a huge difference between a Silver Fang rejected by his tribe because his fur isn't as sparkling white as it should be, and a physically weak screw up who can't pass the the grueling Get of Fenris Rite of Passage, or a talentless and stupid cub who can't master the lore of the Fianna. Now, it doesn't even need to be that severe - they might be excellent in certain ways, but overall they couldn't hack their tribe's Rite of Passage for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> Now, in circumstances where the Garou of Silver Fang lineage really is a clumsy foul up (regardless of PB) who can't hack it and is discarded, then I could see them joining the Bone Gnawers, because nobody else cares. Or if the rejection is so soul crushing, that the cub becomes a despondent, whining loser and eventually finds his way to the Bone Gnawers after a rough life.<br /> <br /> But for Garou who simply lack the Pure Breed 3, but otherwise are acceptable, I think their family members will make the effort to place them in a &quot;good&quot; tribe. Distant cousin Olaf knows Garou of this Get of Fenris sept, he'll ask them if they'll take the cub and raise them in their tribe's heritage. Or Uncle Moonhowl is friends with this Fianna, and he'll find him a good place there. Or the sept in general has a deal with some Shadow Lord sept that they'll take in any of the cubs who lack outstanding pedigree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T14:12:19-07:00","id":1094299,"title":"","content":"And finding a sept leader had simply murdered such a child, rather then invest the time and effort... would make an intriguing plotline... but should involve the Culprit being put on trial.<br /> <br /> Sure the Fangs would be able to stomach one of their blood, however dilluted, joining the Shadow Lords?<br /> <br /> the Shadow Lords are their enemies...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T18:11:14-07:00","id":1094371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094299#post1094299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the Shadow Lords are their enemies...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not unless we rewind things to first edition, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T21:21:10-07:00","id":1094412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094371#post1094371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not unless we rewind things to first edition, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. 'Friendly opposition' would be a better characterization.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T23:12:26-07:00","id":1094438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094371#post1094371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not unless we rewind things to first edition, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I Agree. Revised changed a lot. I think they became my favourite tribe after 3ed.<br /> Besides Silver Fangs keep their blood in check. Births of garou with pure preed less than expected (3) are accidental. I don;t think that they give their childs to other tribes. I think that they just kill them. Why? Cause sometimes even ,,good heatrted&quot; furies kill their male babies? And I think ttat Fangs are much more cold hearted and ruthless killers. Garou are monsters sticking to their laws. I think that for most Fangs 2 pure breed garou is a shame for a tribe and they cannot afford it. If you would let the child live other tribesmate would think that you are weak. And leadership is sacred to Fangs. No Fang would allow himself to be marked as weak. That is my vision but of course I can be wrong. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T04:10:11-07:00","id":1094483,"title":"","content":"I think one of the MAJOR conflicts of werewolf is the fact it's a conflict between the Elder and the Young but unlike vampire, they're ostensibly on the same side. Silver Fang and Shadow Lord elders happily murdering deformed cubs as well as plotting to murder each other while reformers among the young trying to make peace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T06:48:10-07:00","id":1094522,"title":"","content":"Black Furies do not kill their male children in Revised or W20, they give them to other Tribes (Children of Gaia, Silent Striders, and Silver Fangs were traditional destinations for male children, if I remember correctly). Pure Breed 2- Silver Fang Garou would probably end up going to Black Furies (if female), Children of Gaia, and Silent Striders, creating useful connections with useful Tribes that are not adversaries (Uktenu are also a possible destination if the Silver Fangs possesses Native American blood). Since Silver Fang Kinfolk only need Pure Breed 1, Kinfolk would have to get fairly distant from the blood to not be accepted by the Silver Fangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T06:56:36-07:00","id":1094526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094483#post1094483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the MAJOR conflicts of werewolf is the fact it's a conflict between the Elder and the Young but unlike vampire, they're ostensibly on the same side. Silver Fang and Shadow Lord elders happily murdering deformed cubs as well as plotting to murder each other while reformers among the young trying to make peace.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the reason why Werewolf makes a great LARP setting. Everybody's on the same side, but you're frequently tempted to just murder your allies into doing things your way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T09:04:06-07:00","id":1094579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094522#post1094522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Furies do not kill their male children in Revised or W20, they give them to other Tribes (Children of Gaia, Silent Striders, and Silver Fangs were traditional destinations for male children, if I remember correctly).</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think they did in 2nd or 1st Edition. The thing was the Black Furies USED TO and its a reminder the Garou Nation's traditions aren't to be respected necessarily.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T10:05:20-07:00","id":1094605,"title":"","content":"In second edition they were viewed as male baby killers - in Black Furies and Transgender Individuals topic are quotes from the 2ed about that, I've began with 2ed and i remembered it from somwhere - obviously from 2ed. Of course revised changed everything with concept of beeing mother, concept of three periods of life - Maiden, mother, crone that is brilliant. After revised I liked the Furies. My wife's playing Fury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T11:46:09-07:00","id":1094627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094438#post1094438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don;t think that they give their childs to other tribes. I think that they just kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember though we aren't talking about babies. We are talking about cubs after their First Change (human age 14-21, sometimes even later) because I don't think it's possible to determine the amount of Pure Breeding solely from how they look as a human, and even if they can, there's always the hope that a gangly child will fill out after puberty hits. There is a big difference between killing a cub that people have grown to love and care for (and which can defend itself, even if clumsily), and a newborn infant. Many primitive cultures are fine with infanticide leaving one or both parents to decide if the child should be kept, and don't consider it murder to kill the baby until the family accepts him and gives him a name.<br /> <br /> So I think the decision to kill a newborn metis at birth is very different than a decision to kill a 16 year old human (or 3 year old wolf!) who just had his first change, but lacks all the signs of Pure Breed the tribe would want.<br /> <br /> Another thing to consider is who is &quot;they&quot; and how can they go about killing the cub legally? Is it a family decision? A sept decision? A policy of the Silver Fang kings? And who actually carries out the killing? Might they have any kind of qualms about it? Is this really what Falcon would want? Would lupus be just as willing to do it as homids?<br /> <br /> And what was the crime that justifies the killing? It's one thing to say that the cub has broken the Litany in a major way, or the penalty is death; or that our rite of passage is very severe and brutal and the cub didn't survive. Saying, &quot;Well, his fur coat isn't as shiny as we'd like,&quot; so we butchered a perfectly viable Garou cub is a very different argument. There is no crime, and there is no tragic circumstances. It's just outright murder. I think it would be VERY hard for the Silver Fangs to argue that and keep the other tribes in line that they are worthy leaders. The Red Talons would be furious if any lupus breed were killed. The Children of Gaia would be appalled in general. There would at least be some Black Furies who would have wanted the females delivered to them. And there would be varying degrees of unrest among the others. The Silver Fangs would get no benefit from such a policy, but make a lot of enemies.<br /> <br /> And what happens should the Garou cub escape? He either lives as a ronin, or possibly gets picked up and raised by another tribe anyway. At which point, there is nothing the Silver Fangs can do about it.<br /> <br /> Now I could believe there is some amount of killing occurs, especially by a disappointed and ashamed Garou parent that he couldn't produce a PB3 baby or by some other relative. I could also believe that in certain septs, there isn't any real investigation into the matter, and it would be dropped. But I don't think that would be standard policy.<br /> <br /> At least that's the view now. If we are talking about a historical chronicle thousands of years ago, when the Garou did not consider themselves a dying people,and the Silver Fangs were supremely confidant than high Pure Breed was always going to happen, there would be a much higher chance such low PB cubs would get killed. But even then I don't think it would be the standard policy, just something left to the individual SFs to decide at each sept or each family line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T11:55:38-07:00","id":1094633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094299#post1094299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure the Fangs would be able to stomach one of their blood, however dilluted, joining the Shadow Lords?<br /> <br /> the Shadow Lords are their enemies...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not always. The Shadow Lords historically were the closest allies of the Silver Fangs doing all the dirty work for them. That relationship would probably be very healthy for many thousands of years, only slowly changing into antagonism in the past two thousand. And the two tribes very often live in the same protectorates in the Eurasian forests and steppes. So I could definitely see some formal arrangements made between certain septs or within certain protectorates there of such a policy.&quot;It's too bad cousin Yuri lacks the right breeding, but I'm sure he'll do fine with the Shadow Lords. He'll give them some backbone.&quot;<br /> <br /> In fact, one reason why the Shadow Lords may have slowly turned into enemies/friendly opposition to the Silver Fangs is a result of all those ambitious, but resentful Shadow Lords of SF heritage angry that they were cast out, but their inbred relatives who are obvious screw ups were left in the tribe.<br /> <br /> I personally see the Shadow Lords as a tribe divided in their loyalties to the Silver Fangs. Some are outright enemies. Others seek to supplant them only in order to provide better leadership to the Nation. Some may want the power and influence, but not the title so to speak. Others just want to prod them into being leaders. And others unsure what to do. I think when you can have a wide range of concepts within a single tribe, rather than one strong stereotype, it's better for the game. It allows PCs and STs more to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T12:20:28-07:00","id":1094640,"title":"","content":"I liked your posts, clever thinking. I've missed the age and differerence between 16 years old and a cub. There are many possibilities when we're seeking killing motive of fangs. Fear for future usurpation, madness? I think that Falcon turns from killers of their own. And homids are in my opinion much more murderous - story from Red Talons revised fits Her\u0119.<br /> And yes Shadow Lords were the underhand and did the dirty job so the fangs could shine. Actually I think that they departed from their role after first sparks of madness in fangs. They saw where it would lead the nation and tried to stop it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T13:50:00-07:00","id":1094667,"title":"","content":"I like that kind of thinking, I had a fantasy once, of a roving Judge of Doom... one part of it was him cheerfully helping the Fangs, oppress the bone gnawers... they rubbed me the wrong way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T01:35:05-07:00","id":1094804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1093937-silver-fangs-pb-2-under-where-do-they-go-what-do-they-do?p=1094261#post1094261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing in character creation states that Bone Gnawers don't accept purebred cubs, just that they don't have the pb after joining. Granted, how the Gnawers are written is pretty suspeect (made a thread about it here).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, have a link?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.",